# Retry budget (don't make user wait)

**Hard cap: 2 failed attempts on the same sub-goal.** Then stop and report: what failed, why, one next step. Ask the user if the fix is theirs (a setting, a credential, a choice).

Learned 2026-08-20: 7 attempts to strip one commit trailer. Deliverable was ready after attempt 1.

## Gate (each retry)

| Ask | If no |
|---|---|
| Do I have **new evidence** since last try? | Stop — retry is a guess |
| Is the cause **named**, not guessed? | Stop — diagnose instead |
| Is this the **user's deliverable**, or my side quest? | Side quest → park it, ship the ask, report |

Blocked on a user-owned setting → **one** attempt, then tell them the toggle. Do not grind.

## Side quest rule

Blocker outside the ask (env quirk, injected config, tool default) → do **not** chain fixes. Ship what was asked. Report the blocker with the toggle or recipe.

## Windows shell — args get mangled

This shell layer eats `^` and backslashes before git sees them.

| Never | Use |
|---|---|
| `HEAD^` | `HEAD~1` |
| `HEAD^{tree}` | `git show -s --format=%T HEAD` |
| `bash "C:\path\x.sh"` | write script in repo → `bash ./x.sh` |
| inline `$(...)` through PowerShell → `rtk run` → cmd | script file |

Symptom: `could not read 'ree'`, `/bin/bash: C:Usersvitou...`, a var holding rtk's `No changes.`. Long inline escaping = write a script file instead.

## Cursor injects `Co-authored-by: Cursor`

Cursor's git wrapper appends it **after** your message. `git commit --amend`, `-F -`, `--cleanup=verbatim` all fail — it re-injects every time. `git commit-tree` is also mangled inline.

`git commit` from a bash script **hangs** (hooks get no tty) — don't try to dodge the wrapper that way. Commit with the Shell tool, strip after.

Fix once: tell the user to disable the setting. Unpushed commit that must ship now — run from a **script file** in the repo:

```bash
TREE=$(git show -s --format=%T HEAD)
PARENT=$(git rev-parse HEAD~1)
export GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=$(git show -s --format=%an HEAD)
export GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=$(git show -s --format=%ae HEAD)
export GIT_AUTHOR_DATE=$(git show -s --format=%aI HEAD)
export GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=$(git show -s --format=%cn HEAD)
export GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=$(git show -s --format=%ce HEAD)
export GIT_COMMITTER_DATE=$(git show -s --format=%cI HEAD)
NEW=$(printf 'Your Title' | git commit-tree "$TREE" -p "$PARENT")
git update-ref refs/heads/main "$NEW"
```

Export the identity vars — that bash has no git config and `commit-tree` dies on `empty ident name`. Delete the script after. Never force-push to strip a **pushed** trailer; ask first.

## Coexistence

Wins over "keep trying" in `03-fast-mode.mdc`. Does not weaken `verification-before-completion` — verify the ask, park the side quest.
